{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YJgvSYXZX6VPCYB8Ej3Ddw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"context-budget.py — static context-inventory audit (advisory, never blocks).\n3\t\n4\tPLAN-124 WS-4. Stdlib-only, loopback / read-only — like\n5\t``check-staleness.py`` and our other advisory scanners. This tool inventories\n6\tthe **always-loaded / Gate-1 + skill surface** that we re-pay every session\n7\t(CLAUDE.md §0 cache discipline, ~44,786-token gate-boot cost) and produces:\n8\t\n9\t  * a per-category estimated-token table, and\n10\t  * a top-N ranked list of reduction candidates (heaviest files / bloated\n11\t    frontmatter / MCP over-subscription).\n12\t\n13\tIt harvests the **mechanism** from ECC's ``skills/context-budget/SKILL.md``\n14\t(token inventory + heavy-file flagging + top optimizations) re-implemented in\n15\tstdlib Python under our patterns. ECC is MIT; this is a re-implementation, not\n16\ta vendored copy.\n17\t\n18\t## What is inventoried (categories)\n19\t\n20\t| Category    | Surface                                                  |\n21\t|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------|\n22\t| claude_md   | ``CLAUDE.md``                                            |\n23\t| protocol    | ``PROTOCOL.md``                                          |\n24\t| team        | ``.claude/team.md`` + ``.claude/frontend-team.md``       |\n25\t| core_skill  | ``.claude/skills/core/ceo-orchestration/SKILL.md``       |\n26\t| agents      | ``.claude/agents/*.md``                                  |\n27\t| skills      | ``.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md``                           |\n28\t| commands    | ``.claude/commands/*.md``                                |\n29\t| mcp         | MCP subscription surface (``.mcp.json`` / settings)      |\n30\t\n31\t## Heavy-file thresholds (from the ECC reference)\n32\t\n33\t  * agents          > 200 lines\n34\t  * skills          > 400 lines\n35\t  * rules/commands  > 100 lines\n36\t  * frontmatter ``description:`` > 200 chars  (bloated description)\n37\t  * MCP servers     > 5 configured            (over-subscription)\n38\t\n39\t## Token estimate\n40\t\n41\tReuses the repo's documented chars/4 heuristic (see\n42\t``profile-opus-4-7.py:estimate_gate_boot_token_cost`` — \"1 token ≈ 4 chars\").\n43\tThis is an **estimate** for monotonic diff tracking, NOT the Anthropic\n44\ttokenizer. Every report labels it as such.\n45\t\n46\t## Usage\n47\t\n48\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py\n49\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --json\n50\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --top 5\n51\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --repo-root <path>\n52\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --tool-loop-scan <audit-log.jsonl>\n53\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --compact-decision \\\n54\t        --used-tokens 170000 --window-tokens 200000   # D1 auto-compaction probe\n55\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --summarize-decision \\\n56\t        --output-sizes '[12000,800,30000,500]'        # D2 summarize-oldest probe\n57\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --middle-out-decision \\\n58\t        --message-sizes '[50000,800,50000,500]' \\\n59\t        --budget-tokens 60000                          # D5 middle-out ladder probe\n60\t    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --probe-status  # D1/D2/D5 debt state\n61\t\n62\tExit code: always 0 (advisory) — never blocks a session, never writes outside\n63\tstdout. Use ``--strict`` to exit 1 when any heavy-file / over-subscription\n64\tflag fires (for an opt-in advisory CI lint).\n65\t\n66\t## PLAN-153 Wave C item 5 — /context-budget command surface\n67\t\n68\tThe ``/context-budget`` slash command (``.claude/commands/context-budget.md``)\n69\tfronts this CLI. Wave C additions on top of the PLAN-124 inventory:\n70\t\n71\t  * ``savings_top3`` — top-3 progressive-disclosure savings opportunities.\n72\t    Candidate = a SKILL.md over the heavy-skill line threshold with NO\n73\t    ``references/`` dir yet (already-split skills self-retire from the list).\n74\t    The PLAN-153 Wave C item 1 **designated pilots**\n75\t    (``core/testing-strategy``, ``core/security-and-auth``) rank first WHEN\n76\t    the scan finds them still un-split — that ordering is a plan decision,\n77\t    not a pure size rank, and each entry says which rule ranked it.\n78\t  * ``notes`` — honesty block rendered in both outputs: chars/4 is an\n79\t    ESTIMATE (not a tokenizer); this is a STATIC audit (activation-time cost,\n80\t    not runtime usage — retire/merge/improve judgement is /skill-health's\n81\t    scope, and neither tool can measure greenfield domains; PLAN-153 debate A\n82\t    must-fix 4).\n83\t  * Untrusted-data fence (debate B unseen-2): scanned file content is DATA,\n84\t    never instructions. The only free text this report re-displays (MCP\n85\t    server names from config files) passes ``_lib/injection_patterns`` +\n86\t    a conservative charset allowlist; hits render as\n87\t    ``[REDACTED-INJECTION-PATTERN]``. Frontmatter descriptions are only\n88\t    MEASURED (length), never displayed.\n89\t  * ``--scheduled`` — any scheduled wrapper must pass it so\n90\t    ``CEO_SOTA_DISABLE`` is honored.\n91\t\n92\t## PLAN-179 W3 item US11 — probe status (the D1/D2/D5 orphan verdict)\n93\t\n94\tThis file also carries three **decision probes** harvested from PLAN-133\n95\tWave D: D1 (proactive auto-compaction), D2 (summarize oldest verbose\n96\tsubagent outputs), D5 (middle-out degradation ladder). Every one of them is\n97\ta pure decision function plus a ``--*-decision`` CLI mode. **None of them has\n98\ta caller.** An orphan probe that stays silent looks like coverage, so the\n99\tstate is now DECLARED rather than implied, machine-readably, in\n100\t``probe_status()`` — surfaced in ``--json``, in the human report, and via\n101\t``--probe-status``.\n102\t\n103\tSummary of the verdict (full reasoning + measurements:\n104\t``.claude/plans/PLAN-179/orphan-probe-decision.md``):\n105\t\n106\t  * **D1 — KEEP as an exported policy, not as coverage.** Its canonical audit\n107\t    twin (``context_auto_compacted`` / ``context_auto_compact_suppressed``)\n108\t    IS landed in ``.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py``, ``SPEC/v1/\n109\t    audit-log.schema.md`` and ``.claude/data/audit-registry.golden.txt``.\n110\t    Deleting the decision half would orphan a canonical half that only an\n111\t    Owner-GPG ceremony may touch. The consumer that does not exist is a HOST\n112\t    LOOP that owns its own context-management step; Claude Code owns\n113\t    compaction itself, so this repo cannot be that consumer.\n114\t  * **D5 — KEEP, same shape as D1** (``context_middle_out_degraded`` /\n115\t    ``context_middle_out_degrade_failed`` are likewise landed canonical).\n116\t  * **D2 — REMOVE (pending).** D2 has NO canonical twin: its emit actions\n117\t    appear nowhere but this file. Removal must delete the probe AND\n118\t    ``TestSummarizationPolicy`` in ``.claude/scripts/tests/\n119\t    test_context_budget.py`` in one change; that test file was outside the\n120\t    authoring agent's file assignment, so the deletion is scoped and recorded,\n121\t    not half-applied. Deleting the probe alone would turn 144 green tests red.\n122\t\n123\t## Stdlib-only\n124\t\n125\tFilesystem walks + ``json`` for MCP config + a regex frontmatter parse. No\n126\tdeps; never reads outside the given repo-root; never mutates anything.\n127\t\"\"\"\n128\t\n129\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n130\t\n131\timport argparse\n132\timport json\n133\timport os\n134\timport re\n135\timport sys\n136\tfrom pathlib import Path\n137\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n138\t\n139\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n140\t# Heuristic + thresholds\n141\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n142\t\n143\t# Repo-canonical token estimate: 1 token ≈ 4 chars (English-Portuguese mix).\n144\t# Mirrors profile-opus-4-7.py. Estimate only; not the Anthropic tokenizer.\n145\tCHARS_PER_TOKEN = 4\n146\t\n147\t# Heavy-file line thresholds (from the ECC context-budget reference).\n148\tTHRESHOLD_AGENT_LINES = 200\n149\tTHRESHOLD_SKILL_LINES = 400\n150\tTHRESHOLD_RULE_LINES = 100  # commands / rules\n151\t# Bloated frontmatter `description:` length (chars).\n152\tTHRESHOLD_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 200\n153\t# MCP over-subscription: more than this many configured servers.\n154\tTHRESHOLD_MCP_SERVERS = 5\n155\t\n156\t# Category labels (stable keys for --json consumers).\n157\tCAT_CLAUDE_MD = \"claude_md\"\n158\tCAT_PROTOCOL = \"protocol\"\n159\tCAT_TEAM = \"team\"\n160\tCAT_CORE_SKILL = \"core_skill\"\n161\tCAT_AGENTS = \"agents\"\n162\tCAT_SKILLS = \"skills\"\n163\tCAT_COMMANDS = \"commands\"\n164\tCAT_MCP = \"mcp\"\n165\t\n166\t_FRONTMATTER_RE = re.compile(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", re.DOTALL)\n167\t\n168\t\n169\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n170\t# PLAN-153 Wave C — untrusted-data fence (debate B unseen-2)\n171\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n172\t#\n173\t# Everything this tool reads is repo file content — rendered as DATA, never\n174\t# as instructions. The only free-text field re-displayed verbatim-ish is the\n175\t# MCP server name (a key in a JSON config); it passes the harness-mimicry\n176\t# injection scan + a conservative charset allowlist before display (mirrors\n177\t# skill-health.py `fence_token`). Frontmatter descriptions are only MEASURED\n178\t# (length), never displayed, so they need no display fence.\n179\t\n180\t_HOOKS_DIR = str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\")\n181\tif _HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n182\t    sys.path.insert(0, _HOOKS_DIR)\n183\t\n184\ttry:\n185\t    from _lib import injection_patterns as _injection_patterns  # type: ignore\n186\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - exercised via monkeypatch in tests\n187\t    _injection_patterns = None  # type: ignore[assignment]\n188\t\n189\tREDACTED = \"[REDACTED-INJECTION-PATTERN]\"\n190\t\n191\t# Conservative charset for identifier-like fields (MCP server names). No\n192\t# whitespace / angle brackets / pipes survive, so no catalogued injection\n193\t# pattern can survive either; the scanner still runs first when available.\n194\t_TOKEN_ALLOWED = re.compile(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._:/@#+()-]\")\n195\t\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t# Bind extracted declarations to this original CLI module namespace.\n199\tfrom _lib._context_budget_parts import install as _install_context_parts\n200\t_install_context_parts(globals(), (\n201\t    \"inventory\", \"compaction\", \"summarization\", \"middle_out\", \"status\",\n202\t))\n203\tdel _install_context_parts\n204\t\n205\tdef _cli(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n206\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n207\t        description=\"ceo-orchestration context-budget audit (advisory, \"\n208\t                    \"read-only, never blocks)\",\n209\t    )\n210\t    parser.add_argument(\n211\t        \"--repo-root\", default=\".\", help=\"project root (default: cwd)\")\n212\t    parser.add_argument(\n213\t        \"--json\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"machine-readable JSON output\")\n214\t    parser.add_argument(\n215\t        \"--top\", type=int, default=10,\n216\t        help=\"how many top reduction candidates to rank (default: 10)\")\n217\t    parser.add_argument(\n218\t        \"--strict\", action=\"store_true\",\n219\t        help=\"exit 1 if any flag fires (opt-in advisory CI lint)\")\n220\t    parser.add_argument(\n221\t        \"--scheduled\", action=\"store_true\",\n222\t        help=\"mark this run as scheduled machinery (honors CEO_SOTA_DISABLE)\")\n223\t    parser.add_argument(\n224\t        \"--tool-loop-scan\", metavar=\"AUDIT_LOG\", default=None,\n225\t        help=\"(P3) flag N identical consecutive tool-calls in an audit-log \"\n226\t             \"JSONL file, then exit\")\n227\t    parser.add_argument(\n228\t        \"--loop-min\", type=int, default=3,\n229\t        help=\"min consecutive identical tool-calls to flag a loop (default: 3)\")\n230\t    # PLAN-133 D1 — auto-compaction decision probe (advisory; default-OFF unless\n231\t    # CEO_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD is set in the environment).\n232\t    parser.add_argument(\n233\t        \"--compact-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n234\t        help=\"(D1) print the proactive auto-compaction decision for a context \"\n235\t             \"snapshot, then exit. Default-OFF: requires CEO_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD.\")\n236\t    parser.add_argument(\"--used-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n237\t                        help=\"(D1) current context usage in tokens\")\n238\t    parser.add_argument(\"--window-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n239\t                        help=\"(D1) model context window in tokens\")\n240\t    parser.add_argument(\"--reclaimable-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n241\t                        help=\"(D1) estimated tokens a compaction would free\")\n242\t    parser.add_argument(\"--armed\", dest=\"armed\", action=\"store_true\", default=True,\n243\t                        help=\"(D1) re-arm flag is set (default)\")\n244\t    parser.add_argument(\"--disarmed\", dest=\"armed\", action=\"store_false\",\n245\t                        help=\"(D1) re-arm flag is cleared (post-compaction)\")\n246\t    parser.add_argument(\"--turns-since-compaction\", type=int, default=None,\n247\t                        help=\"(D1) turns elapsed since the last compaction\")\n248\t    # PLAN-133 D2 — oldest-verbose-output summarization decision probe\n249\t    # (advisory; default-OFF unless CEO_SUMMARIZE_OLDEST is set). Reads an\n250\t    # ordered list of per-output token sizes (oldest first) from a JSON file or\n251\t    # inline, and prints the summarization plan, then exits.\n252\t    parser.add_argument(\n253\t        \"--summarize-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n254\t        help=\"(D2) print the oldest-verbose-output summarization plan for a \"\n255\t             \"list of subagent output token-sizes, then exit. Default-OFF: \"\n256\t             \"requires CEO_SUMMARIZE_OLDEST.\")\n257\t    parser.add_argument(\n258\t        \"--output-sizes\", metavar=\"JSON\", default=None,\n259\t        help=\"(D2) JSON array of per-output est-token sizes (OLDEST FIRST), \"\n260\t             \"e.g. '[12000, 800, 30000, 500]'\")\n261\t    parser.add_argument(\n262\t        \"--output-sizes-file\", metavar=\"PATH\", default=None,\n263\t        help=\"(D2) path to a JSON file holding the per-output size array\")\n264\t    # PLAN-133 D5 — middle-out degradation ladder decision probe (advisory;\n265\t    # default-OFF unless CEO_MIDDLE_OUT_DEGRADE is set). Reads an ordered list of\n266\t    # per-message token sizes (oldest first) + a budget, and prints the\n267\t    # degradation plan, then exits. Decision only — never elides anything.\n268\t    parser.add_argument(\n269\t        \"--middle-out-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n270\t        help=\"(D5) print the middle-out degradation plan for a list of message \"\n271\t             \"token-sizes + a token budget, then exit. Default-OFF: requires \"\n272\t             \"CEO_MIDDLE_OUT_DEGRADE.\")\n273\t    parser.add_argument(\n274\t        \"--message-sizes\", metavar=\"JSON\", default=None,\n275\t        help=\"(D5) JSON array of per-message est-token sizes (OLDEST FIRST), \"\n276\t             \"e.g. '[50000, 800, 50000, 500]'\")\n277\t    parser.add_argument(\n278\t        \"--message-sizes-file\", metavar=\"PATH\", default=None,\n279\t        help=\"(D5) path to a JSON file holding the per-message size array\")\n280\t    parser.add_argument(\n281\t        \"--budget-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n282\t        help=\"(D5) the token budget the assembled context must fit within\")\n283\t    # PLAN-179 W3 US11 — print the declared D1/D2/D5 probe status and exit.\n284\t    parser.add_argument(\n285\t        \"--probe-status\", action=\"store_true\",\n286\t        help=\"(US11) print the declared orphan-probe status for the D1/D2/D5 \"\n287\t             \"decision probes (verdict, missing consumer, removal scope), \"\n288\t             \"then exit. Descriptive only.\")\n289\t    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n290\t\n291\t    # CEO_SOTA_DISABLE contract: any *scheduled* machinery must honor it.\n292\t    if args.scheduled and os.environ.get(\"CEO_SOTA_DISABLE\"):\n293\t        print(\"[context-budget] skipped: CEO_SOTA_DISABLE is set \"\n294\t              \"(scheduled run)\")\n295\t        return 0\n296\t\n297\t    # Clamp a negative --top to 0 (least-surprising): a negative limit would\n298\t    # otherwise SKIP the slice and return ALL candidates plus print a\n299\t    # nonsensical \"top -N\" header. 0 cleanly means \"rank nothing\".\n300\t    if args.top is not None and args.top < 0:\n301\t        args.top = 0\n302\t\n303\t    # US11 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Pure description of the\n304\t    # probe debt; reads nothing, writes nothing, always exit 0.\n305\t    if args.probe_status:\n306\t        print(json.dumps(probe_status(), indent=2))\n307\t        return 0\n308\t\n309\t    # D1 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n310\t    # prints the decision dict, never compacts, never emits, always exit 0.\n311\t    if args.compact_decision:\n312\t        decision = decide_compaction(\n313\t            args.used_tokens,\n314\t            args.window_tokens,\n315\t            reclaimable_tokens=args.reclaimable_tokens,\n316\t            armed=args.armed,\n317\t            turns_since_last_compaction=args.turns_since_compaction,\n318\t        )\n319\t        print(json.dumps(decision, indent=2))\n320\t        return 0\n321\t\n322\t    # D2 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n323\t    # prints the summarization plan, never summarizes, never emits, exit 0.\n324\t    if args.summarize_decision:\n325\t        sizes: Any = []\n326\t        raw = None\n327\t        if args.output_sizes_file:\n328\t            raw = _read_text(Path(args.output_sizes_file))\n329\t        elif args.output_sizes is not None:\n330\t            raw = args.output_sizes\n331\t        if raw is not None:\n332\t            try:\n333\t                sizes = json.loads(raw)\n334\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n335\t                sizes = []  # fail-open: malformed input ⇒ empty (disabled-ish)\n336\t        plan = decide_summarization(sizes)\n337\t        print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))\n338\t        return 0\n339\t\n340\t    # D5 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n341\t    # prints the degradation plan, never elides, never emits, exit 0.\n342\t    if args.middle_out_decision:\n343\t        msg_sizes: Any = []\n344\t        raw = None\n345\t        if args.message_sizes_file:\n346\t            raw = _read_text(Path(args.message_sizes_file))\n347\t        elif args.message_sizes is not None:\n348\t            raw = args.message_sizes\n349\t        if raw is not None:\n350\t            try:\n351\t                msg_sizes = json.loads(raw)\n352\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n353\t                msg_sizes = []  # fail-open: malformed input ⇒ empty\n354\t        budget = args.budget_tokens if args.budget_tokens is not None else 0\n355\t        plan = decide_middle_out_degradation(msg_sizes, budget)\n356\t        print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))\n357\t        return 0\n358\t\n359\t    # P3 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory.\n360\t    if args.tool_loop_scan is not None:\n361\t        result = scan_tool_loops(Path(args.tool_loop_scan), min_run=args.loop_min)\n362\t        if args.json:\n363\t            print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n364\t        else:\n365\t            print(_render_loops_human(result))\n366\t        # Advisory: exit 0 unless --strict and loops were found.\n367\t        if args.strict and result.get(\"loops\"):\n368\t            return 1\n369\t        return 0\n370\t\n371\t    repo = Path(args.repo_root).resolve()\n372\t    report = build_inventory(repo, top=args.top)\n373\t\n374\t    if args.json:\n375\t        print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n376\t    else:\n377\t        print(_render_human(report, args.top))\n378\t\n379\t    if args.strict and report[\"flag_count\"] > 0:\n380\t        return 1\n381\t    return 0\n382\t\n383\t\n384\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n385\t    sys.exit(_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n386\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7affb10d-4e4f-46c9-8efb-a709552287db","uuid":"da050cbe-cc3a-4252-ba13-42d816d4c21e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:47:33.345Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/context-budget.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"context-budget.py — static context-inventory audit (advisory, never blocks).\n\nPLAN-124 WS-4. Stdlib-only, loopback / read-only — like\n``check-staleness.py`` and our other advisory scanners. This tool inventories\nthe **always-loaded / Gate-1 + skill surface** that we re-pay every session\n(CLAUDE.md §0 cache discipline, ~44,786-token gate-boot cost) and produces:\n\n  * a per-category estimated-token table, and\n  * a top-N ranked list of reduction candidates (heaviest files / bloated\n    frontmatter / MCP over-subscription).\n\nIt harvests the **mechanism** from ECC's ``skills/context-budget/SKILL.md``\n(token inventory + heavy-file flagging + top optimizations) re-implemented in\nstdlib Python under our patterns. ECC is MIT; this is a re-implementation, not\na vendored copy.\n\n## What is inventoried (categories)\n\n| Category    | Surface                                                  |\n|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------|\n| claude_md   | ``CLAUDE.md``                                            |\n| protocol    | ``PROTOCOL.md``                                          |\n| team        | ``.claude/team.md`` + ``.claude/frontend-team.md``       |\n| core_skill  | ``.claude/skills/core/ceo-orchestration/SKILL.md``       |\n| agents      | ``.claude/agents/*.md``                                  |\n| skills      | ``.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md``                           |\n| commands    | ``.claude/commands/*.md``                                |\n| mcp         | MCP subscription surface (``.mcp.json`` / settings)      |\n\n## Heavy-file thresholds (from the ECC reference)\n\n  * agents          > 200 lines\n  * skills          > 400 lines\n  * rules/commands  > 100 lines\n  * frontmatter ``description:`` > 200 chars  (bloated description)\n  * MCP servers     > 5 configured            (over-subscription)\n\n## Token estimate\n\nReuses the repo's documented chars/4 heuristic (see\n``profile-opus-4-7.py:estimate_gate_boot_token_cost`` — \"1 token ≈ 4 chars\").\nThis is an **estimate** for monotonic diff tracking, NOT the Anthropic\ntokenizer. Every report labels it as such.\n\n## Usage\n\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --json\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --top 5\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --repo-root <path>\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --tool-loop-scan <audit-log.jsonl>\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --compact-decision \\\n        --used-tokens 170000 --window-tokens 200000   # D1 auto-compaction probe\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --summarize-decision \\\n        --output-sizes '[12000,800,30000,500]'        # D2 summarize-oldest probe\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --middle-out-decision \\\n        --message-sizes '[50000,800,50000,500]' \\\n        --budget-tokens 60000                          # D5 middle-out ladder probe\n    python3 .claude/scripts/context-budget.py --probe-status  # D1/D2/D5 debt state\n\nExit code: always 0 (advisory) — never blocks a session, never writes outside\nstdout. Use ``--strict`` to exit 1 when any heavy-file / over-subscription\nflag fires (for an opt-in advisory CI lint).\n\n## PLAN-153 Wave C item 5 — /context-budget command surface\n\nThe ``/context-budget`` slash command (``.claude/commands/context-budget.md``)\nfronts this CLI. Wave C additions on top of the PLAN-124 inventory:\n\n  * ``savings_top3`` — top-3 progressive-disclosure savings opportunities.\n    Candidate = a SKILL.md over the heavy-skill line threshold with NO\n    ``references/`` dir yet (already-split skills self-retire from the list).\n    The PLAN-153 Wave C item 1 **designated pilots**\n    (``core/testing-strategy``, ``core/security-and-auth``) rank first WHEN\n    the scan finds them still un-split — that ordering is a plan decision,\n    not a pure size rank, and each entry says which rule ranked it.\n  * ``notes`` — honesty block rendered in both outputs: chars/4 is an\n    ESTIMATE (not a tokenizer); this is a STATIC audit (activation-time cost,\n    not runtime usage — retire/merge/improve judgement is /skill-health's\n    scope, and neither tool can measure greenfield domains; PLAN-153 debate A\n    must-fix 4).\n  * Untrusted-data fence (debate B unseen-2): scanned file content is DATA,\n    never instructions. The only free text this report re-displays (MCP\n    server names from config files) passes ``_lib/injection_patterns`` +\n    a conservative charset allowlist; hits render as\n    ``[REDACTED-INJECTION-PATTERN]``. Frontmatter descriptions are only\n    MEASURED (length), never displayed.\n  * ``--scheduled`` — any scheduled wrapper must pass it so\n    ``CEO_SOTA_DISABLE`` is honored.\n\n## PLAN-179 W3 item US11 — probe status (the D1/D2/D5 orphan verdict)\n\nThis file also carries three **decision probes** harvested from PLAN-133\nWave D: D1 (proactive auto-compaction), D2 (summarize oldest verbose\nsubagent outputs), D5 (middle-out degradation ladder). Every one of them is\na pure decision function plus a ``--*-decision`` CLI mode. **None of them has\na caller.** An orphan probe that stays silent looks like coverage, so the\nstate is now DECLARED rather than implied, machine-readably, in\n``probe_status()`` — surfaced in ``--json``, in the human report, and via\n``--probe-status``.\n\nSummary of the verdict (full reasoning + measurements:\n``.claude/plans/PLAN-179/orphan-probe-decision.md``):\n\n  * **D1 — KEEP as an exported policy, not as coverage.** Its canonical audit\n    twin (``context_auto_compacted`` / ``context_auto_compact_suppressed``)\n    IS landed in ``.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py``, ``SPEC/v1/\n    audit-log.schema.md`` and ``.claude/data/audit-registry.golden.txt``.\n    Deleting the decision half would orphan a canonical half that only an\n    Owner-GPG ceremony may touch. The consumer that does not exist is a HOST\n    LOOP that owns its own context-management step; Claude Code owns\n    compaction itself, so this repo cannot be that consumer.\n  * **D5 — KEEP, same shape as D1** (``context_middle_out_degraded`` /\n    ``context_middle_out_degrade_failed`` are likewise landed canonical).\n  * **D2 — REMOVE (pending).** D2 has NO canonical twin: its emit actions\n    appear nowhere but this file. Removal must delete the probe AND\n    ``TestSummarizationPolicy`` in ``.claude/scripts/tests/\n    test_context_budget.py`` in one change; that test file was outside the\n    authoring agent's file assignment, so the deletion is scoped and recorded,\n    not half-applied. Deleting the probe alone would turn 144 green tests red.\n\n## Stdlib-only\n\nFilesystem walks + ``json`` for MCP config + a regex frontmatter parse. No\ndeps; never reads outside the given repo-root; never mutates anything.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Heuristic + thresholds\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Repo-canonical token estimate: 1 token ≈ 4 chars (English-Portuguese mix).\n# Mirrors profile-opus-4-7.py. Estimate only; not the Anthropic tokenizer.\nCHARS_PER_TOKEN = 4\n\n# Heavy-file line thresholds (from the ECC context-budget reference).\nTHRESHOLD_AGENT_LINES = 200\nTHRESHOLD_SKILL_LINES = 400\nTHRESHOLD_RULE_LINES = 100  # commands / rules\n# Bloated frontmatter `description:` length (chars).\nTHRESHOLD_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 200\n# MCP over-subscription: more than this many configured servers.\nTHRESHOLD_MCP_SERVERS = 5\n\n# Category labels (stable keys for --json consumers).\nCAT_CLAUDE_MD = \"claude_md\"\nCAT_PROTOCOL = \"protocol\"\nCAT_TEAM = \"team\"\nCAT_CORE_SKILL = \"core_skill\"\nCAT_AGENTS = \"agents\"\nCAT_SKILLS = \"skills\"\nCAT_COMMANDS = \"commands\"\nCAT_MCP = \"mcp\"\n\n_FRONTMATTER_RE = re.compile(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", re.DOTALL)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAN-153 Wave C — untrusted-data fence (debate B unseen-2)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n#\n# Everything this tool reads is repo file content — rendered as DATA, never\n# as instructions. The only free-text field re-displayed verbatim-ish is the\n# MCP server name (a key in a JSON config); it passes the harness-mimicry\n# injection scan + a conservative charset allowlist before display (mirrors\n# skill-health.py `fence_token`). Frontmatter descriptions are only MEASURED\n# (length), never displayed, so they need no display fence.\n\n_HOOKS_DIR = str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\")\nif _HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, _HOOKS_DIR)\n\ntry:\n    from _lib import injection_patterns as _injection_patterns  # type: ignore\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - exercised via monkeypatch in tests\n    _injection_patterns = None  # type: ignore[assignment]\n\nREDACTED = \"[REDACTED-INJECTION-PATTERN]\"\n\n# Conservative charset for identifier-like fields (MCP server names). No\n# whitespace / angle brackets / pipes survive, so no catalogued injection\n# pattern can survive either; the scanner still runs first when available.\n_TOKEN_ALLOWED = re.compile(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._:/@#+()-]\")\n\n\n\n# Bind extracted declarations to this original CLI module namespace.\nfrom _lib._context_budget_parts import install as _install_context_parts\n_install_context_parts(globals(), (\n    \"inventory\", \"compaction\", \"summarization\", \"middle_out\", \"status\",\n))\ndel _install_context_parts\n\ndef _cli(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"ceo-orchestration context-budget audit (advisory, \"\n                    \"read-only, never blocks)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--repo-root\", default=\".\", help=\"project root (default: cwd)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--json\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"machine-readable JSON output\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--top\", type=int, default=10,\n        help=\"how many top reduction candidates to rank (default: 10)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--strict\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"exit 1 if any flag fires (opt-in advisory CI lint)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--scheduled\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"mark this run as scheduled machinery (honors CEO_SOTA_DISABLE)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--tool-loop-scan\", metavar=\"AUDIT_LOG\", default=None,\n        help=\"(P3) flag N identical consecutive tool-calls in an audit-log \"\n             \"JSONL file, then exit\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--loop-min\", type=int, default=3,\n        help=\"min consecutive identical tool-calls to flag a loop (default: 3)\")\n    # PLAN-133 D1 — auto-compaction decision probe (advisory; default-OFF unless\n    # CEO_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD is set in the environment).\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--compact-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"(D1) print the proactive auto-compaction decision for a context \"\n             \"snapshot, then exit. Default-OFF: requires CEO_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--used-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n                        help=\"(D1) current context usage in tokens\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--window-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n                        help=\"(D1) model context window in tokens\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--reclaimable-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n                        help=\"(D1) estimated tokens a compaction would free\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--armed\", dest=\"armed\", action=\"store_true\", default=True,\n                        help=\"(D1) re-arm flag is set (default)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--disarmed\", dest=\"armed\", action=\"store_false\",\n                        help=\"(D1) re-arm flag is cleared (post-compaction)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--turns-since-compaction\", type=int, default=None,\n                        help=\"(D1) turns elapsed since the last compaction\")\n    # PLAN-133 D2 — oldest-verbose-output summarization decision probe\n    # (advisory; default-OFF unless CEO_SUMMARIZE_OLDEST is set). Reads an\n    # ordered list of per-output token sizes (oldest first) from a JSON file or\n    # inline, and prints the summarization plan, then exits.\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--summarize-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"(D2) print the oldest-verbose-output summarization plan for a \"\n             \"list of subagent output token-sizes, then exit. Default-OFF: \"\n             \"requires CEO_SUMMARIZE_OLDEST.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--output-sizes\", metavar=\"JSON\", default=None,\n        help=\"(D2) JSON array of per-output est-token sizes (OLDEST FIRST), \"\n             \"e.g. '[12000, 800, 30000, 500]'\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--output-sizes-file\", metavar=\"PATH\", default=None,\n        help=\"(D2) path to a JSON file holding the per-output size array\")\n    # PLAN-133 D5 — middle-out degradation ladder decision probe (advisory;\n    # default-OFF unless CEO_MIDDLE_OUT_DEGRADE is set). Reads an ordered list of\n    # per-message token sizes (oldest first) + a budget, and prints the\n    # degradation plan, then exits. Decision only — never elides anything.\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--middle-out-decision\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"(D5) print the middle-out degradation plan for a list of message \"\n             \"token-sizes + a token budget, then exit. Default-OFF: requires \"\n             \"CEO_MIDDLE_OUT_DEGRADE.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--message-sizes\", metavar=\"JSON\", default=None,\n        help=\"(D5) JSON array of per-message est-token sizes (OLDEST FIRST), \"\n             \"e.g. '[50000, 800, 50000, 500]'\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--message-sizes-file\", metavar=\"PATH\", default=None,\n        help=\"(D5) path to a JSON file holding the per-message size array\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--budget-tokens\", type=int, default=None,\n        help=\"(D5) the token budget the assembled context must fit within\")\n    # PLAN-179 W3 US11 — print the declared D1/D2/D5 probe status and exit.\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--probe-status\", action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"(US11) print the declared orphan-probe status for the D1/D2/D5 \"\n             \"decision probes (verdict, missing consumer, removal scope), \"\n             \"then exit. Descriptive only.\")\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    # CEO_SOTA_DISABLE contract: any *scheduled* machinery must honor it.\n    if args.scheduled and os.environ.get(\"CEO_SOTA_DISABLE\"):\n        print(\"[context-budget] skipped: CEO_SOTA_DISABLE is set \"\n              \"(scheduled run)\")\n        return 0\n\n    # Clamp a negative --top to 0 (least-surprising): a negative limit would\n    # otherwise SKIP the slice and return ALL candidates plus print a\n    # nonsensical \"top -N\" header. 0 cleanly means \"rank nothing\".\n    if args.top is not None and args.top < 0:\n        args.top = 0\n\n    # US11 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Pure description of the\n    # probe debt; reads nothing, writes nothing, always exit 0.\n    if args.probe_status:\n        print(json.dumps(probe_status(), indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    # D1 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n    # prints the decision dict, never compacts, never emits, always exit 0.\n    if args.compact_decision:\n        decision = decide_compaction(\n            args.used_tokens,\n            args.window_tokens,\n            reclaimable_tokens=args.reclaimable_tokens,\n            armed=args.armed,\n            turns_since_last_compaction=args.turns_since_compaction,\n        )\n        print(json.dumps(decision, indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    # D2 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n    # prints the summarization plan, never summarizes, never emits, exit 0.\n    if args.summarize_decision:\n        sizes: Any = []\n        raw = None\n        if args.output_sizes_file:\n            raw = _read_text(Path(args.output_sizes_file))\n        elif args.output_sizes is not None:\n            raw = args.output_sizes\n        if raw is not None:\n            try:\n                sizes = json.loads(raw)\n            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n                sizes = []  # fail-open: malformed input ⇒ empty (disabled-ish)\n        plan = decide_summarization(sizes)\n        print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    # D5 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory. Advisory + read-only:\n    # prints the degradation plan, never elides, never emits, exit 0.\n    if args.middle_out_decision:\n        msg_sizes: Any = []\n        raw = None\n        if args.message_sizes_file:\n            raw = _read_text(Path(args.message_sizes_file))\n        elif args.message_sizes is not None:\n            raw = args.message_sizes\n        if raw is not None:\n            try:\n                msg_sizes = json.loads(raw)\n            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n                msg_sizes = []  # fail-open: malformed input ⇒ empty\n        budget = args.budget_tokens if args.budget_tokens is not None else 0\n        plan = decide_middle_out_degradation(msg_sizes, budget)\n        print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    # P3 fold-in mode — independent of the inventory.\n    if args.tool_loop_scan is not None:\n        result = scan_tool_loops(Path(args.tool_loop_scan), min_run=args.loop_min)\n        if args.json:\n            print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n        else:\n            print(_render_loops_human(result))\n        # Advisory: exit 0 unless --strict and loops were found.\n        if args.strict and result.get(\"loops\"):\n            return 1\n        return 0\n\n    repo = Path(args.repo_root).resolve()\n    report = build_inventory(repo, top=args.top)\n\n    if args.json:\n        print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    else:\n        print(_render_human(report, args.top))\n\n    if args.strict and report[\"flag_count\"] > 0:\n        return 1\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n","numLines":386,"startLine":1,"totalLines":386}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YJgvSYXZX6VPCYB8Ej3Ddw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1GVYi4wByWQ6UgBnByX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NhD5zo1vFsTn5Sk4seBXH1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7627,"cache_read_input_tokens":114070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7627},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7affb10d-4e4f-46c9-8efb-a709552287db","uuid":"ff7ac227-749b-4dd5-bfb0-461446f467ef","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:47:33.898Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1GVYVRgVJXtxB2FK14p","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NhD5zo1vFsTn5Sk4seBXH1":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NhD5zo1vFsTn5Sk4seBXH1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"ceo-cost-transcripts.py — cost/token report derived from harness-native\n3\ttranscripts (``message.usage`` per assistant turn), NOT the audit log.\n4\t\n5\t## Why this exists (PLAN-186 W0, S339)\n6\t\n7\t``ceo-cost.py`` and ``budget-summary.py``'s audit-log rollup report\n8\t``$0.00`` over 30 days because the audit log is a *governance* log (spawns,\n9\tvetoes, edits, ceremonies) — it is not a token ledger. The real spend lives\n10\tin the harness-native transcripts under\n11\t``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/*.jsonl`` (the main/\"assento\" sessions) and\n12\t``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` (spawned\n13\tsub-agents, both plain Task-tool and Workflow rails). Each ``type ==\n14\t\"assistant\"`` record carries a full ``message.usage`` snapshot: fresh\n15\tinput, output, and prompt-cache read/write (split 5-minute / 1-hour TTL).\n16\t\n17\tThis is documented in ``docs/research/s339-orchestrator-study/\n18\t05-finops-routing.md`` (P0-1, §1, §Metodologia) — that report's own\n19\tscratchpad-local aggregator produced **$11,137.97** over 2026-08-03 →\n20\t2026-09-02. This script is the in-tree, tested, stdlib-only version of\n21\tthat instrument.\n22\t\n23\t``budget-summary.py`` already reads *some* native transcripts\n24\t(``_read_native_spawn`` / ``collect_native_spawns``, lines 920-1200) but\n25\tonly under ``<session>/subagents/**`` — it never reads the top-level\n26\t``<session>.jsonl`` files, so it is structurally blind to the \"assento\"\n27\t(main session) spend, which the S339 report measured at 71% of the total.\n28\tThis script reads BOTH trees and separates them.\n29\t\n30\t## Pricing contract\n31\t\n32\tDefault pricing is an EMBEDDED table (``_EMBEDDED_PRICING`` below),\n33\tsourced from the S339 report §1.2/§1.4, itself derived from\n34\t``docs/provider-pricing.md`` (primary table + cache-tier multipliers,\n35\tlines ~130-153) and ``budget-summary.py``'s\n36\t``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` (the per-model cache-read\n37\texceptions, mirrored below; every other model at 0.10x base; cache\n38\tWRITE is 1.25x base at the 5-minute TTL and 2.00x base at the 1-hour\n39\tTTL — these multipliers are a\n40\tstructural constant, not something ``cost-table.yaml`` carries).\n41\t\n42\t``--pricing PATH`` (default ``cost-table.yaml`` next to this script)\n43\tattempts to load base ``input_per_mtok`` / ``output_per_mtok`` rows from\n44\tthat file's mini-YAML ``models:`` block. Two cases:\n45\t\n46\t- **Format doesn't match at all** (file missing, unreadable, no\n47\t  ``models:`` section found, zero rows extracted): fall back to the\n48\t  fully embedded table wholesale. ``cost-table.yaml`` in this repo has\n49\t  NO cache-read/cache-write columns at all — this instrument's whole\n50\t  point is cache-aware pricing, so a table that cannot express that is,\n51\t  by construction, a format mismatch for this use case; the embedded\n52\t  table is the one that can.\n53\t- **Format parses AND the path is the untouched default**: rows load\n54\t  from the file, then the Owner-ratified corrections in\n55\t  ``_RATIFIED_OVERRIDES_FOR_DEFAULT_TABLE`` are layered on top — but\n56\t  ONLY where the parsed row actually DIFFERS from the ratified rate.\n57\t  As of ``b6dce78`` the in-tree ``cost-table.yaml`` already carries the\n58\t  ratified ``claude-sonnet-5`` $2/$10 row, so on the default path the\n59\t  correction is currently a NO-OP and ``source`` says so. An\n60\t  unconditional overwrite would be worse than useless: it would print\n61\t  \"ratified correction\" while correcting nothing, and the day the\n62\t  table is legitimately refreshed it would silently mask the new rate.\n63\t  An EXPLICIT ``--pricing`` path supplied by the caller is trusted\n64\t  as-is, with no correction at all — the caller opted into a specific\n65\t  pricing config on purpose.\n66\t\n67\tCache-read/write multipliers are ALWAYS the structural constants above,\n68\tregardless of which base table is in play, applied per-model (the\n69\t``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` exceptions act on cache read only).\n70\t\n71\t## Corpus contract\n72\t\n73\t- Dedup key: ``message.id`` when present (an API response's usage\n74\t  snapshot is identical across every content-block JSONL line the\n75\t  harness writes for that one message — thinking/text/tool_use blocks\n76\t  each get their own line, all carrying the SAME ``message.usage``);\n77\t  falls back to ``requestId`` + record ``uuid`` when ``message.id`` is\n78\t  absent. The S339 report's methodology names a\n79\t  ``(requestId, apiBlockIndex, message.id)`` key; ``apiBlockIndex`` was\n80\t  not observed in this harness version's on-disk schema, so the key\n81\t  degrades to what IS observed without inventing a field.\n82\t- Role: \"assento\" for non-sidechain assistant turns in a top-level\n83\t  ``<session>.jsonl``; \"subagent\" for every assistant turn under\n84\t  ``<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` regardless of its own\n85\t  ``isSidechain`` value (path-shape is the classifier, mirroring\n86\t  ``budget-summary.py``'s rail-by-path doctrine — the corpus has no\n87\t  reliable field for this). A sidechain turn inside a top-level file (not\n88\t  observed in this corpus, but not structurally impossible) is skipped\n89\t  rather than double-counted: any Task-tool sub-dispatch already has its\n90\t  own dedicated ``agent-*.jsonl``.\n91\t- Never touches ``iterations`` on a usage record (it double-counts\n92\t  retries — same exclusion the S339 report's methodology names).\n93\t- A JSON-parse failure on a candidate line is skipped and counted, never\n94\t  raised. An ``unresolved`` model id (not found in the active pricing\n95\t  table, after stripping a trailing ``[..]`` context-window suffix such\n96\t  as ``[1m]``) is bucketed and reported with its token totals — never\n97\t  silently priced at $0 as if it were a genuine zero-cost turn, and never\n98\t  guessed.\n99\t\n100\t## Routing invariant (PLAN-186 AC-13, S361)\n101\t\n102\tEVERY execution of this instrument also ASSERTS, from runtime data only,\n103\tthat the model a spawn was SERVED equals the model its call site DECLARED\n104\t(``transcript_rollup()['routing']``: the CLI report, the ``--json`` payload,\n105\tand ``collect()``/``render_block()`` for ``ceo-cost.py`` and\n106\t``budget-summary.py``). ADR-144:140 measured ``agent(..., {model})`` routing\n107\ton ONE harness build (n=2) and carries no forward guarantee; a proof taken\n108\tonce at land time cannot see the harness going back to ``inherit`` later.\n109\t\n110\t- DECLARED is the ``model`` key of the spawn's ``agent-<id>.meta.json``\n111\t  sidecar: what the call actually passed. It is never read from the text of\n112\t  a script (an instrument that predicts code from text does not converge).\n113\t  Absent or ``inherit`` means NO claim at the site: counted, never a\n114\t  violation.\n115\t- SERVED is ``message.model`` of the paired ``agent-<id>.jsonl``, never the\n116\t  agent's self-report, read through the SAME ``scan_files()``/``dedup()`` as\n117\t  the cost report -- with ONE difference: the served model is a fact of the\n118\t  TURN, not of its bill, so the routing read lifts the ``usage``\n119\t  requirement. A turn the cost report drops for want of ``usage`` (null,\n120\t  absent, empty) is still read here, and an assistant record that cannot be\n121\t  read at all is counted (INCONCLUSIVE), never silently skipped. Chunks of\n122\t  one message resolve to the TERMINAL chunk (highest ``output_tokens``; on a\n123\t  tie the LATER line in file order). A message whose chunks disagree about\n124\t  the model is counted in ``chunk_model_splits`` (informational) when the\n125\t  terminal chunk can be elected from complete information; if one of those\n126\t  chunks has NO ``output_tokens`` the terminal cannot be proven, it is\n127\t  counted in ``chunk_terminal_unprovable``, the group is EXCLUDED from the\n128\t  comparison (its guessed terminal can neither raise a violation nor vouch\n129\t  for the routing) and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE -- never GREEN, and never\n130\t  RED on that group's account; a RED can only come from another group whose\n131\t  terminal is proven. ``<synthetic>`` is a harness pseudo-model and is\n132\t  ignored.\n133\t- EVERY string taken from a transcript or a sidecar is made printable where\n134\t  it enters the instrument (non-printable characters become ``?``): a model\n135\t  id, a session id, a label or an archetype name cannot forge a verdict line\n136\t  or drive a terminal in ANY renderer.\n137\t- A WINDOW decides first. A sidecar the check cannot trust (unreadable,\n138\t  refused, or a declaration it cannot classify) gates a window only if its\n139\t  spawn has a turn inside it; one from outside is counted as\n140\t  ``out_of_window`` and never reaches the verdict. The same holds record by\n141\t  record: an unreadable assistant record with a valid timestamp OUTSIDE the\n142\t  window leaves before it is counted; only what has no temporal position at\n143\t  all (a torn line, no timestamp) or sits inside the window can make the\n144\t  verdict INCONCLUSIVE, and where that makes a spawn's placement unprovable\n145\t  the check fails closed. The ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters stay\n146\t  corpus-wide.\n147\t- LABEL is the sidecar ``description`` (the Workflow ``label``; the native\n148\t  spawn's ``description``).\n149\t- ALIAS -> FAMILY, not alias -> id. ``opus|sonnet|haiku|fable`` are matched\n150\t  by FAMILY, derived from the fleet tables and never retyped; a full id is\n151\t  matched EXACTLY (a ``-YYYYMMDD`` date suffix is tolerated). A pinned\n152\t  alias -> id table was refused on evidence: on one harness the same\n153\t  ``sonnet`` was served as ``claude-sonnet-5`` and later as\n154\t  ``claude-sonnet-5-5``, so such a table is red the day the substrate\n155\t  re-points the alias and green over the very hole it has to see. The\n156\t  alias -> served pairs actually observed are PRINTED, never judged.\n157\t- SECOND PREDICATE (the AC-10 requirement named for whoever closes AC-13):\n158\t  a spawn whose archetype (``customAgentType``, else ``agentType``) is in\n159\t  ``VETO_FLOOR_ROLES`` must be served inside ``VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`` --\n160\t  MEMBERSHIP, never a family prefix -- declared or not. Both sets are\n161\t  imported from ``_lib.agent_frontmatter``, never retyped. Declared ==\n162\t  served is silent about the floor (``model: sonnet`` on a VETO spawn\n163\t  matches itself and is still a breach), which is why this is a second\n164\t  predicate and not a corollary of the first.\n165\t- Verdicts, worst first: RED (a violation), INCONCLUSIVE (something the\n166\t  check could not read or classify, named), VACUOUS (nothing was compared:\n167\t  a vacuous GREEN is refused), GREEN. The exit code stays 0 so the cost\n168\t  report is never broken by a routing finding; ``--assert-routing`` turns\n169\t  the verdict into a gate: 0 GREEN, 1 RED, 3 not proven (INCONCLUSIVE or\n170\t  VACUOUS). Out of scope, declared: the seat (no sidecar), spawns that\n171\t  declare nothing, an archetype that the sidecar does not record (the\n172\t  persona-injected ``general-purpose`` rail), and whether a site's\n173\t  ``model:`` is the RIGHT one for its task class (AC-3a / W1).\n174\t\n175\tPRE-REGISTERED DEATH CRITERIA -- fixed here before the first real run;\n176\tchanging any number is a plan amendment, never an edit in passing.\n177\t\n178\t  K-A (the detector dies: rebuild or retire it, never tune around it)\n179\t    K-A1 positive control: the synthetic pair in\n180\t         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n181\t         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n182\t         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n183\t    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n184\t         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n185\t         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n186\t         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n187\t         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n188\t         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n189\t    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n190\t         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n191\t         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n192\t         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n193\t         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n194\t         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n195\t         no suppression list in this file.\n196\t  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n197\t    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n198\t         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n199\t         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n200\t         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n201\t         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n202\t         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n203\t         passes.\n204\t    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n205\t         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n206\t         registered by the permanent detector\").\n207\t\n208\tStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n209\t\"\"\"\n210\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n211\t\n212\timport argparse\n213\timport glob\n214\timport json\n215\timport os\n216\timport re\n217\timport sys\n218\timport time\n219\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n220\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n221\tfrom pathlib import Path\n222\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n223\t\n224\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n225\t# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n226\t# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n227\t# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n228\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n230\t_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n231\t_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n232\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n233\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n234\t\n235\ttry:\n236\t    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\n237\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n238\t    _rp = None\n239\t\n240\t\n241\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n242\t# Pricing tables\n243\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n247\t# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\n248\tfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n249\t\n250\t_install_parts(globals(), (\n251\t    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n252\t))\n253\t\n254\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n255\t    sys.exit(main())\n256\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7affb10d-4e4f-46c9-8efb-a709552287db","uuid":"67486c1f-780a-4bd2-a545-e7d3e1c80f2c","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:47:33.902Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"ceo-cost-transcripts.py — cost/token report derived from harness-native\ntranscripts (``message.usage`` per assistant turn), NOT the audit log.\n\n## Why this exists (PLAN-186 W0, S339)\n\n``ceo-cost.py`` and ``budget-summary.py``'s audit-log rollup report\n``$0.00`` over 30 days because the audit log is a *governance* log (spawns,\nvetoes, edits, ceremonies) — it is not a token ledger. The real spend lives\nin the harness-native transcripts under\n``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/*.jsonl`` (the main/\"assento\" sessions) and\n``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` (spawned\nsub-agents, both plain Task-tool and Workflow rails). Each ``type ==\n\"assistant\"`` record carries a full ``message.usage`` snapshot: fresh\ninput, output, and prompt-cache read/write (split 5-minute / 1-hour TTL).\n\nThis is documented in ``docs/research/s339-orchestrator-study/\n05-finops-routing.md`` (P0-1, §1, §Metodologia) — that report's own\nscratchpad-local aggregator produced **$11,137.97** over 2026-08-03 →\n2026-09-02. This script is the in-tree, tested, stdlib-only version of\nthat instrument.\n\n``budget-summary.py`` already reads *some* native transcripts\n(``_read_native_spawn`` / ``collect_native_spawns``, lines 920-1200) but\nonly under ``<session>/subagents/**`` — it never reads the top-level\n``<session>.jsonl`` files, so it is structurally blind to the \"assento\"\n(main session) spend, which the S339 report measured at 71% of the total.\nThis script reads BOTH trees and separates them.\n\n## Pricing contract\n\nDefault pricing is an EMBEDDED table (``_EMBEDDED_PRICING`` below),\nsourced from the S339 report §1.2/§1.4, itself derived from\n``docs/provider-pricing.md`` (primary table + cache-tier multipliers,\nlines ~130-153) and ``budget-summary.py``'s\n``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` (the per-model cache-read\nexceptions, mirrored below; every other model at 0.10x base; cache\nWRITE is 1.25x base at the 5-minute TTL and 2.00x base at the 1-hour\nTTL — these multipliers are a\nstructural constant, not something ``cost-table.yaml`` carries).\n\n``--pricing PATH`` (default ``cost-table.yaml`` next to this script)\nattempts to load base ``input_per_mtok`` / ``output_per_mtok`` rows from\nthat file's mini-YAML ``models:`` block. Two cases:\n\n- **Format doesn't match at all** (file missing, unreadable, no\n  ``models:`` section found, zero rows extracted): fall back to the\n  fully embedded table wholesale. ``cost-table.yaml`` in this repo has\n  NO cache-read/cache-write columns at all — this instrument's whole\n  point is cache-aware pricing, so a table that cannot express that is,\n  by construction, a format mismatch for this use case; the embedded\n  table is the one that can.\n- **Format parses AND the path is the untouched default**: rows load\n  from the file, then the Owner-ratified corrections in\n  ``_RATIFIED_OVERRIDES_FOR_DEFAULT_TABLE`` are layered on top — but\n  ONLY where the parsed row actually DIFFERS from the ratified rate.\n  As of ``b6dce78`` the in-tree ``cost-table.yaml`` already carries the\n  ratified ``claude-sonnet-5`` $2/$10 row, so on the default path the\n  correction is currently a NO-OP and ``source`` says so. An\n  unconditional overwrite would be worse than useless: it would print\n  \"ratified correction\" while correcting nothing, and the day the\n  table is legitimately refreshed it would silently mask the new rate.\n  An EXPLICIT ``--pricing`` path supplied by the caller is trusted\n  as-is, with no correction at all — the caller opted into a specific\n  pricing config on purpose.\n\nCache-read/write multipliers are ALWAYS the structural constants above,\nregardless of which base table is in play, applied per-model (the\n``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` exceptions act on cache read only).\n\n## Corpus contract\n\n- Dedup key: ``message.id`` when present (an API response's usage\n  snapshot is identical across every content-block JSONL line the\n  harness writes for that one message — thinking/text/tool_use blocks\n  each get their own line, all carrying the SAME ``message.usage``);\n  falls back to ``requestId`` + record ``uuid`` when ``message.id`` is\n  absent. The S339 report's methodology names a\n  ``(requestId, apiBlockIndex, message.id)`` key; ``apiBlockIndex`` was\n  not observed in this harness version's on-disk schema, so the key\n  degrades to what IS observed without inventing a field.\n- Role: \"assento\" for non-sidechain assistant turns in a top-level\n  ``<session>.jsonl``; \"subagent\" for every assistant turn under\n  ``<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` regardless of its own\n  ``isSidechain`` value (path-shape is the classifier, mirroring\n  ``budget-summary.py``'s rail-by-path doctrine — the corpus has no\n  reliable field for this). A sidechain turn inside a top-level file (not\n  observed in this corpus, but not structurally impossible) is skipped\n  rather than double-counted: any Task-tool sub-dispatch already has its\n  own dedicated ``agent-*.jsonl``.\n- Never touches ``iterations`` on a usage record (it double-counts\n  retries — same exclusion the S339 report's methodology names).\n- A JSON-parse failure on a candidate line is skipped and counted, never\n  raised. An ``unresolved`` model id (not found in the active pricing\n  table, after stripping a trailing ``[..]`` context-window suffix such\n  as ``[1m]``) is bucketed and reported with its token totals — never\n  silently priced at $0 as if it were a genuine zero-cost turn, and never\n  guessed.\n\n## Routing invariant (PLAN-186 AC-13, S361)\n\nEVERY execution of this instrument also ASSERTS, from runtime data only,\nthat the model a spawn was SERVED equals the model its call site DECLARED\n(``transcript_rollup()['routing']``: the CLI report, the ``--json`` payload,\nand ``collect()``/``render_block()`` for ``ceo-cost.py`` and\n``budget-summary.py``). ADR-144:140 measured ``agent(..., {model})`` routing\non ONE harness build (n=2) and carries no forward guarantee; a proof taken\nonce at land time cannot see the harness going back to ``inherit`` later.\n\n- DECLARED is the ``model`` key of the spawn's ``agent-<id>.meta.json``\n  sidecar: what the call actually passed. It is never read from the text of\n  a script (an instrument that predicts code from text does not converge).\n  Absent or ``inherit`` means NO claim at the site: counted, never a\n  violation.\n- SERVED is ``message.model`` of the paired ``agent-<id>.jsonl``, never the\n  agent's self-report, read through the SAME ``scan_files()``/``dedup()`` as\n  the cost report -- with ONE difference: the served model is a fact of the\n  TURN, not of its bill, so the routing read lifts the ``usage``\n  requirement. A turn the cost report drops for want of ``usage`` (null,\n  absent, empty) is still read here, and an assistant record that cannot be\n  read at all is counted (INCONCLUSIVE), never silently skipped. Chunks of\n  one message resolve to the TERMINAL chunk (highest ``output_tokens``; on a\n  tie the LATER line in file order). A message whose chunks disagree about\n  the model is counted in ``chunk_model_splits`` (informational) when the\n  terminal chunk can be elected from complete information; if one of those\n  chunks has NO ``output_tokens`` the terminal cannot be proven, it is\n  counted in ``chunk_terminal_unprovable``, the group is EXCLUDED from the\n  comparison (its guessed terminal can neither raise a violation nor vouch\n  for the routing) and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE -- never GREEN, and never\n  RED on that group's account; a RED can only come from another group whose\n  terminal is proven. ``<synthetic>`` is a harness pseudo-model and is\n  ignored.\n- EVERY string taken from a transcript or a sidecar is made printable where\n  it enters the instrument (non-printable characters become ``?``): a model\n  id, a session id, a label or an archetype name cannot forge a verdict line\n  or drive a terminal in ANY renderer.\n- A WINDOW decides first. A sidecar the check cannot trust (unreadable,\n  refused, or a declaration it cannot classify) gates a window only if its\n  spawn has a turn inside it; one from outside is counted as\n  ``out_of_window`` and never reaches the verdict. The same holds record by\n  record: an unreadable assistant record with a valid timestamp OUTSIDE the\n  window leaves before it is counted; only what has no temporal position at\n  all (a torn line, no timestamp) or sits inside the window can make the\n  verdict INCONCLUSIVE, and where that makes a spawn's placement unprovable\n  the check fails closed. The ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters stay\n  corpus-wide.\n- LABEL is the sidecar ``description`` (the Workflow ``label``; the native\n  spawn's ``description``).\n- ALIAS -> FAMILY, not alias -> id. ``opus|sonnet|haiku|fable`` are matched\n  by FAMILY, derived from the fleet tables and never retyped; a full id is\n  matched EXACTLY (a ``-YYYYMMDD`` date suffix is tolerated). A pinned\n  alias -> id table was refused on evidence: on one harness the same\n  ``sonnet`` was served as ``claude-sonnet-5`` and later as\n  ``claude-sonnet-5-5``, so such a table is red the day the substrate\n  re-points the alias and green over the very hole it has to see. The\n  alias -> served pairs actually observed are PRINTED, never judged.\n- SECOND PREDICATE (the AC-10 requirement named for whoever closes AC-13):\n  a spawn whose archetype (``customAgentType``, else ``agentType``) is in\n  ``VETO_FLOOR_ROLES`` must be served inside ``VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`` --\n  MEMBERSHIP, never a family prefix -- declared or not. Both sets are\n  imported from ``_lib.agent_frontmatter``, never retyped. Declared ==\n  served is silent about the floor (``model: sonnet`` on a VETO spawn\n  matches itself and is still a breach), which is why this is a second\n  predicate and not a corollary of the first.\n- Verdicts, worst first: RED (a violation), INCONCLUSIVE (something the\n  check could not read or classify, named), VACUOUS (nothing was compared:\n  a vacuous GREEN is refused), GREEN. The exit code stays 0 so the cost\n  report is never broken by a routing finding; ``--assert-routing`` turns\n  the verdict into a gate: 0 GREEN, 1 RED, 3 not proven (INCONCLUSIVE or\n  VACUOUS). Out of scope, declared: the seat (no sidecar), spawns that\n  declare nothing, an archetype that the sidecar does not record (the\n  persona-injected ``general-purpose`` rail), and whether a site's\n  ``model:`` is the RIGHT one for its task class (AC-3a / W1).\n\nPRE-REGISTERED DEATH CRITERIA -- fixed here before the first real run;\nchanging any number is a plan amendment, never an edit in passing.\n\n  K-A (the detector dies: rebuild or retire it, never tune around it)\n    K-A1 positive control: the synthetic pair in\n         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n         no suppression list in this file.\n  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n         passes.\n    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n         registered by the permanent detector\").\n\nStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport glob\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n\ntry:\n    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n    _rp = None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Pricing tables\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\nfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n\n_install_parts(globals(), (\n    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":256,"startLine":1,"totalLines":256}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NhD5zo1vFsTn5Sk4seBXH1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
