repr wrapper on `__repr__`. The wrapper is created by dataclasses/reprlib, gets the component's `__module__` through wraps (or an explicit copy), and needs the global `_thread` (3.9-3.11) or `get_ident` (3.12+). Neither exists in the ceo-cost-transcripts.py namespace. Result: repr() and str() of UsageRecord, ScanCounters, PricingResult and Priced raise NameError. I found no production caller that formats these objects, so the damage is limited to debugging and test diagnostics. Fix: rebind only when `method.__code__.co_filename` is the component's own file, or skip dataclass-generated members.\n2. Honesty, stale location comments in the moved text: middle_out.py:22, summarization.py:21 and compaction.py:20 say the code \"lives here in `scripts/`\"; status.py:24 refers to the probes \"above\"; pricing.py:171 and routing_helpers.py:127 point to \"the module docstring\", which now sits in the facade. Fix: update the pointers.\n3. verdicts_b.py:698 (bound by _installer_write_safety/__init__.py:45-48): its `__all__` does not exclude `_commands` / `_commands_name`, so a module object and a string leak into the facade namespace, and commands' classes get cloned a second time. Harmless today, but it widens the re-exported surface. Fix: add both names to the exclusion tuple.\n\nClean in this payload: the context-budget extraction (middle_out, summarization, status), the cost-transcripts window, dedup and routing logic, and the installer-census engine, commands and model logic match the facades' documented contracts. I found nothing that disables a governance hook, changes model or effort, or blocks a legitimate session.","decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","sentence":"No declared condition is false against this payload and I found no P0; the one undeclared P1 is latent and fails closed in a maintainer-only tool (on the facade, Incomplete no longer subclasses ParseError after cloning), and it has to be carried as a signed annex finding or fixed."},"ttft_ms":93311,"type":"result",